[Event "Pirc: Austrian Attack"]

{The Pirc lets White build a big centre and then attacks it with ...c5, ...e5 and the g7-bishop.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... d6 {The Pirc. The pawn on d6 controls e5.}
2. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
2... Nf6 {Hits e4. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
3. Nc3 {Defends. The knight on c3 controls d5.}
3... g6 {[%csl Gg7] Fianchetto.}
4. f4 {The Austrian Attack. The pawn on f4 controls e5.}
4... Bg7 {Develops.}
5. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
5... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
 (5... c5 {The immediate strike at d4. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
6. dxc5 {Takes. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d6.}
6... Qa5 {[%cal Ga5c5] Pins the knight and regains c5. The queen on a5 eyes the pawn on c5 and the knight on c3.}
)
6. Bd3 {Develops.}
6... Na6 {Prepares ...c5.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... c5 {[%cal Gc5d4] Hits the centre. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
8. d5 {Gains space.} *

[Event "Pirc: 150 Attack & Classical"]

{Against Be3/Qd2 Black plays ...c6 and ...b5. Against the Classical, develop calmly.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... d6 {Pirc. The pawn on d6 controls e5.}
2. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
2... Nf6 {Hits e4. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
3. Nc3 {Defends. The knight on c3 controls d5.}
3... g6 {Fianchetto.}
4. Be3 {The 150 Attack.}
 (4. Nf3 {The Classical. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
4... Bg7 {Develops.}
5. Be2 {Develops.}
5... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... c6 {Prepares ...b5 or ...Qc7. The pawn on c6 controls d5.}
7. a4 {Stops ...b5.}
7... Nbd7 {Develops. The knight on d7 controls e5.}
)
 (4. Bg5 {The Byrne. The bishop on g5 eyes the knight on f6.}
4... Bg7 {Develops.}
5. Qd2 {Prepares Bh6.}
5... h6 {Kicks the bishop. The pawn on h6 eyes the bishop on g5.}
6. Bh4 {Keeps the pin. The bishop on h4 eyes the knight on f6.}
6... c6 {Flexible. The pawn on c6 controls d5.}
)
4... c6 {Prepares ...b5. The pawn on c6 controls d5.}
5. Qd2 {Prepares Bh6.}
5... b5 {[%cal Gb5b4] Queenside counterplay.}
6. Bd3 {Develops. The bishop on d3 eyes the pawn on b5.}
6... Nbd7 {Develops. The knight on d7 controls e5.}
7. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
7... e5 {Hits the centre. The pawn on e5 eyes the pawn on d4.} *
